The fill that turns tracing on leaves the turn owing from where it was in the tick.
Under tracing the clock is the tick count, so QEMU would charge the first traced tick less than the host;
a traced turn is charged from the tick.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a traced turn is charged from within a tick

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -327,8 +327,6 @@ static struct thread *unit_first(uint32_t unit)
 void sched_accounts_fill(void)
 {
     struct core *core = core_self();
-    /* The fill clears what the turn owed, too. */
-    core->turn_from = clock_offset();
     core->nearest_release = sched_ticks + NEAREST_NONE;
     for (uint32_t i = 0; i < TIME_UNITS; i++) {
         LOOP_BOUND(TIME_UNITS);
